+# Ramification at infinity
+
+For a nonconstant function on a smooth curve, the degree of the function-field
+extension equals the degree of its pole divisor. Applying the fundamental
+ramification–inertia identity to the prime `(X)` of `k[X]`, embedded by
+`X ↦ f⁻¹`, identifies its ramification indices with pole orders and its
+inertia degrees with residue-field degrees.
