+# q-th roots of multiplication coordinates
+
+Over a finite field `K` of cardinality `q`, taking the `q`-th power of a
+polynomial equals expansion by `q`. Thus a polynomial in the image of
+`Polynomial.expand K q` has a polynomial `q`-th root, obtained by choosing
+an expansion preimage. Evaluation at the function-field coordinate preserves
+this identity.
+
+Applied to the numerator and denominator division polynomials, these roots
+give explicit preimages under Frobenius of the multiplication coordinates.
+The coordinate constructions retain their polynomial membership and
+nonvanishing hypotheses; the characteristic-two and characteristic-three
+specializations supply the corresponding concrete witnesses.
