+# The Picard dual isogeny
+
+For an elliptic-curve endomorphism `α` with a coordinate-ring comorphism,
+transporting ideal extension along `κ : E ≃ Pic⁰(E)` defines the Picard dual.
+Transporting the relative ideal norm defines the point-group pushforward.
+The norm–extension identity gives `picPushforward ∘ picDual = [deg α]`.
+Under the naturality relation between the point map and `κ`, this yields
+`α ∘ α̂ = [deg α]`; surjectivity gives the companion relation by cancellation.
+
+At rational points, residue degree one identifies the relative ideal norm
+with contraction. This proves the corresponding naturality reduction
+without a perfectness assumption on the function field.
 
